# Conventions — TypeScript code style

## Context

The app is TypeScript-strict (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is on) and follows a
small, consistent style so the codebase stays predictable. See
`app/src/reducer.ts` and `app/src/actions.ts` for the pattern to match.

## Rule

- **Named exports only** — no `export default`.
- **No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`.** If a type is genuinely unknown, model it
  properly instead of widening or suppressing.
- **Immutable state updates** — use spread/`map`/`filter` to produce new
  objects/arrays; never mutate `state`, `state.tasks`, or a `Task` in place.
- **File names: kebab-case** (e.g. `text-utils.ts`); type/interface names:
  PascalCase (e.g. `AppState`, `Task`).

## How to verify

1. `rg -n "export default" app --glob '*.{ts,tsx}'` — no matches.
2. `rg -n "\bany\b|@ts-ignore" app --glob '*.{ts,tsx}'` — no matches (outside
   comments explaining why one was deliberately avoided).
3. `cd app && npm run typecheck` passes with strict mode on.
4. New `.ts`/`.tsx` files under `app` use kebab-case names.
